# The Enigma Jewel // Locus of Enlightenment. The Jewel enters tapped (turn 1). On turn 7 Bot1 crafts it ("Craft with four
# or more nonlands with activated abilities {8}{U}"), paying {C}{C} of the cost with the Jewel's own mana (the ruling: a
# craft ability is an activated ability) and exiling the Walking Ballista from the graveyard and Goblin Bombardment, Mox
# Ruby and Mox Jet from the battlefield; the Ornithopter (no activated ability) and a land are no materials. Locus returns
# transformed, untapped, with the abilities of the four cards (CR 702.167c). Bot1 activates the Bombardment's
# "Sacrifice a creature: ... 1 damage to any target" of Locus at Bot2; Locus's trigger copies it (CR 707.10) and the copy
# is given a new target, Bot1 (CR 707.10c). The copy was not activated, so it does not trigger Locus again: each player
# takes exactly 1. That ability may be activated only once each turn: refused with a second Ornithopter to sacrifice,
# and offered again on turn 9, where Bot1 keeps the copy's target (Bot2 takes 2 more).

